+
+## JSON Patch (RFC 6902)
+
+```ts
+import { applyPatch } from "./src/index.ts";
+
+applyPatch({ a: [1, 2] }, [
+  { op: "add", path: "/a/-", value: 3 },
+  { op: "test", path: "/a/0", value: 1 },
+  { op: "move", from: "/a/1", path: "/b" },
+]); // { a: [1, 3], b: 2 }
+```
+
+`applyPatch(document, patch)` applies the operations (`add`, `remove`, `replace`, `move`, `copy`, `test`) in
+order and returns the result as a new value; the document and the patch are never mutated. It throws a
+`JsonPatchError` when the patch is invalid (not an array, unknown `op`, missing or invalid `path`/`from`/`value`)
+or when an operation fails (target missing, bad array index, `move` into its own child, failed `test`). Nothing
+is returned in that case, so a failed patch has no partial effect.
