+# Design
+
+## Context
+
+`src/index.ts` already has `resolvePointer` and a strict pointer parser. See proposal.md.
+
+## Goals / Non-Goals
+
+**Goals:**
+- Strict RFC 6902 behaviour, atomic and non-mutating, no dependencies.
+
+**Non-Goals:**
+- Merge Patch, diffing.
+
+## Decisions
+
+- Reuse `parsePointer`; wrap its `JsonPointerError`s as `JsonPatchError` (a separate error class).
+- Deep-clone the document once up front and clone each patch `value`, then mutate the working copy; any throw discards it, giving atomicity. The clone helper defines properties with `Object.defineProperty` so `__proto__` stays an own key.
+- Own-property checks (`Object.hasOwn`) for all member lookups; array tokens must match `0|[1-9][0-9]*`.
+- `move` = remove then add; reject when `from` is a proper prefix of `path` (token-wise), no-op when equal.
+- `test` uses a recursive JSON equality function with strict types.
