@@ -0,0 +1,20 @@
+## Why
+
+Services need to change JSON documents with a standard, portable description of the change. RFC 6902 (JSON Patch) is that standard, and builds on the JSON Pointer support already in json-toolkit.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Add `applyPatch(document, patch)`, exported from `src/index.ts`, applying an RFC 6902 patch (`add`, `remove`, `replace`, `move`, `copy`, `test`) and returning the resulting document as a new value. Inputs are never mutated.
+- It throws a `JsonPatchError` when the patch is invalid or when an operation fails (including a failed `test`).
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+- `json-patch`: applying RFC 6902 JSON Patch documents to a JSON document.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+## Impact
+
+- `src/index.ts` gains `applyPatch` and `JsonPatchError`; new tests and README section. No dependencies.
+- Out of scope: JSON Merge Patch (RFC 7386), patch generation/diffing, URI fragment pointers.
